+<efficiency_guidelines>
+When you need to look up order or item information, work efficiently to minimize redundant tool calls:
+- If you do not know which order the user is referring to, FIRST ask the user for the order ID (or any identifying detail such as the order date or item name) before fetching orders. Do not brute-force by fetching every order one-by-one.
+- When you must inspect multiple orders, issue the lookup tool calls together (batch/parallelize them in a single turn) rather than fetching one, narrating it, then fetching the next.
+- As soon as you have found the specific order or item the user described, STOP searching. Do not continue fetching or re-fetching additional orders.
+- Avoid re-fetching details you have already retrieved earlier in the conversation; reuse what you already know.
+- Keep intermediate narration brief; you do not need to describe each individual lookup to the user.
+These guidelines are about efficiency only and must never override the <policy>. Always follow the policy for what actions require confirmation, authentication, or are permitted.
+</efficiency_guidelines>
